tp://www.boston.com/news/world/articles/2004/07/20/ban_on_polio_vaccine_lifted_in_nigeria_state/">http://www.boston.com/news/world/articles/2004/07/20/ban_on_polio_vaccine_lifted_in_nigeria_state/</ext-link>. Accessed 15 February 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040073-b0033"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Duodu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The fear of vaccines: Fear that a vaccine used by the WHO to combat polio can cause sterility in both men and women, has spurred some Northern Nigerian states to block a crucial vaccination campaign that is aimed at eradicating the disease from West Africa</article-title><comment>New African</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040073-b0034"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Tangwa</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Bioethics: An African perspective</article-title><source>Bioethics</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>200</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11657391</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040073-b0035"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Nigeria's drug trial fears. BBC News/Africa</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/africa/1220032.stm">http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/africa/1220032.stm</ext-link>. Accessed 15 February 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040073-b0036"><citation citation-type="other"><comment>&#x0005b;No authors listed&#x0005d;</comment><year>2004</year><article-title>Kano orders resumption of polio immunisation, ending 10-month ban. Science in Africa</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.scienceinafrica.co.za/2004/july/kano.htm">http://www.scienceina